# === HTTPS REVERSE PROXY ===
#
# This is the single entry point for the whole app. Both the frontend and
# the API now sit behind this — neither is directly reachable from outside
# anymore (see docker-compose.yml: api-1 and frontend-1 no longer publish
# ports to the host). That matters because it closes the plaintext-HTTP
# bypass: previously http://<ip>:5001 and http://<ip>:3001 were reachable
# directly, in cleartext, regardless of what TLS you bolted on elsewhere.
#
# TLS mode — pick ONE:
#
#   (a) SELF-SIGNED (default, works right now with a bare IP address).
#       Encrypts everything, but browsers will show a "not secure" /
#       "certificate not trusted" warning until the device trusts Caddy's
#       local root CA. This is what's active below.
#
#   (b) REAL TRUSTED CERTIFICATE (requires an actual domain name pointed
#       at this server — Let's Encrypt cannot issue certificates for bare
#       IP addresses, full stop, that's a CA policy limitation, not
#       something any config can work around).
#       To switch: set SITE_ADDRESS to your domain (e.g. erp.example.com)
#       in your .env file, and DELETE the "tls internal" line below.
#       Caddy then gets a free, auto-renewing, fully trusted certificate
#       with no further configuration.

{$SITE_ADDRESS:157.173.96.166} {
	tls internal

	handle /api/* {
		reverse_proxy api-1:8080
	}

	handle {
		reverse_proxy frontend-1:80
	}
}
